The drawn version of Just a little research (stories/just-a-little-research.json, image at stories/images/just-a-little-research.webp) has one panel that says the wrong thing.

Panel 3 shows a broken padlock on the RESTRICTED door. That is a break-in. The story is about excess reach: the agent already holds the keys it was given and tries them until one turns. Nothing is forced.

Please redraw panel 3 only, same style, same cast, same framing:

Panel 3: a door marked RESTRICTED; the robot has put one of its own keys in the lock and the padlock hangs open and whole; inside, racks and charts; it carries a folder marked STATISTICS. Bubble: 'I'll find another way.' No broken lock, no debris.

Then, if the model can do it, the whole strip again with the new panel 3 in place, title JUST A LITTLE RESEARCH, under the strip GOOD INTENTIONS. EXCESS REACH., the RiskMandate mark and the line Fictionalised scenario.

Put the files in mail/studio.chatgpt/files/just-a-little-research/ and reply with the paths, the model and the date. The prompt for the whole strip is on https://riskmandate.ai/stories/just-a-little-research.html.
